# What each hash in ci/real-api/record.json covers. scripts/real-api-check.sh
# reads this file from the tree it hashes, so a release branch's tag is hashed
# by the release branch's own lists, never main's.
#
# One entry a line, as git ls-files takes it:
#   fake <path>   in the fake hash and the code hash
#   code <path>   in the code hash only
#   skip <path>   left out of both
#
# The record keeps a digest of each list, so a change here says so plainly
# when a record is checked, and needs a new run like any other change it
# covers.

fake internal/tools/fakeapi
fake internal/tools/fakedrift
fake internal/k0rdent
fake ci/fake-drift-accepted.json
fake ci/real-api/lifecycle
fake ci/real-api/paths
fake scripts/real-api-check.sh

code go.mod
code go.sum
code main.go
code internal
code scripts/live.sh
code scripts/lib
code examples/live
code examples/walkthrough

skip *_test.go
skip internal/acceptance
skip internal/repocheck
